    {
      "id": "claim_d21593be066342fab0ee72a08a5de1e2",
      "statement": "The Pregel algorithm executes graphs in supersteps: atomic synchronization barriers where nodes read state, execute in parallel, write results, and advance to the next superstep only if channels were updated or nodes request further execution.",
