    {
      "id": "claim_489a014b4fd1408ab092faf9b4f187ef",
      "statement": "Channel reducers aggregate concurrent writes in one superstep: when multiple tasks write to the same channel, the reducer is invoked with the current value and a sequence of updates, and must be associative so replaying batches of writes produces the same result regardless of batching granularity.",
